# Two ways to attach. "{B}{B}: Attach this Equipment to target creature you control" is a plain activated ability, usable at
# instant speed: in Bot2's upkeep on turn four it puts the Plating on Bot1's first Ornithopter, a 6/2 (six artifacts Bot1
# controls: three Moxen, the Plating, two Ornithopters; Bot2's Sol Ring, cast first, is not counted). "Equip {1}" is
# sorcery speed (CR 702.6a), so it is refused in the upkeep (the refusal) and used in Bot1's main phase on turn five
# (the positive control), where it moves the Plating to the second Ornithopter and the first loses the bonus. Equip
# targets a creature you control only: Bot2's Ornithopter is refused beside it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Swamp
Cranial Plating
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Swamp x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Sol Ring
Mountain
Ornithopter
Mountain x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cranial Plating.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Cranial Plating.Activate(Ability: Equip {1})
Bot1.Battlefield.Cranial Plating.Activate(Ornithopter#1; Ability: {B}{B})
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#3.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Cranial Plating.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Power = 6
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Cranial Plating.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Ability: Equip {1})
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Cranial Plating.Activate(Ornithopter#2; Ability: Equip {1})
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Power = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Power = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
